## Server and Client Component Rules

- Keep data fetching and static layout in Server Components.
- Add `"use client"` only when needed.
- Do not mark full pages as client components unless required.
- Do not use hooks like `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRouter`, or browser APIs inside Server Components.
- Move interactive UI into separate Client Components.
- Pass only serializable props from Server Components to Client Components.

## UI and Design Rules

### Design Direction

- Premium beauty brand feel.
- Elegant and modern layouts.
- Clean white-space usage.
- Soft visual hierarchy.
- Feminine, polished, salon-style experience.

### Layout Rules

- Mobile-first responsive design.
- Proper container widths.
- Consistent spacing scale.
- Sticky actions only when necessary.
- Avoid cluttered layouts.
- Use clean sections with clear spacing.

### Typography

- Consistent font hierarchy.
- Readable text sizes.
- Balanced line heights.
- Proper heading structure.
- Use H1 only once per page.
- Keep headings meaningful and semantic.

### Components

- Reusable components preferred.
- Avoid duplicate buttons, cards, forms, and sections.
- Keep components predictable.
- Use composition instead of copy-paste.
- Keep UI variants simple and maintainable.

### Animations

- Keep animations subtle.
- Avoid heavy motion.
- Prefer smooth transitions.
- Do not add unnecessary animation libraries.
- Respect performance and accessibility.

### Forms

- Clear validation states.
- Accessible inputs.
- Proper loading and disabled states.
- Use semantic labels.
- Show helpful error messages.
- Avoid confusing form behavior.

### Accessibility

- Proper semantic HTML.
- Keyboard accessibility.
- Sufficient contrast.
- Proper focus states.
- Use aria attributes only when needed.
- Buttons should be buttons, links should be links.

## Styling Rules

- Use Tailwind CSS classes.
- Avoid inline styles unless absolutely necessary.
- Keep spacing, radius, shadow, and border styles consistent.
- Prefer soft borders, rounded corners, and subtle shadows.
- Use premium brand colors consistently.

## Brand Direction

- Primary: Rose / Pink
- Secondary: Warm Beige
- Accent: Gold
- Background: Soft Ivory
- Text: Deep Brown / Charcoal
- Muted: Warm Gray

## Output Rules

- Always provide file/folder structure first.
- Then provide complete code file by file.
- Explain imports clearly.
- Do not remove existing working code unnecessarily.
- Do not rename existing files, routes, types, or components unless required.
- Keep code production-ready, clean, and easy to maintain.
